{"content":[{"c":["AIJALON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. City located in a valley 15 miles (24 kilometers) northwest of Jerusalem (at modern Yalo) and originally allotted to Dan’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.42","r":"Josh.19.42","rawR":"Josh.19.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.42","value":"Josh.19.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:42"},"). Aijalon was designated as one of four levitical cities in Dan’s area (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.24","r":"Josh.21.24","rawR":"Josh.21.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.24","value":"Josh.21.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:24"},") and was later made a city of refuge by Ephraim’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.69","r":"1Chr.6.69","rawR":"1Chr.6.69","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.69","value":"1Chr.6.69"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:69"},"). Dan’s tribe had by then migrated north, having been unable to occupy its southerly allotment, including Aijalon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.34-36","r":"Judg.1.34-36","rawR":"Judg.1.34-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.34-36","value":"Judg.1.34-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:34-36"},"). Near Aijalon, Saul and Jonathan won a victory over the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.31","r":"1Sam.14.31","rawR":"1Sam.14.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.31","value":"1Sam.14.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 14:31"},"). Members of Benjamin’s tribe occupied it at one time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.13","r":"1Chr.8.13","rawR":"1Chr.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.13","value":"1Chr.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["When the kingdom was divided after Solomon’s death, Aijalon, on the northwest border of the southern kingdom, was fortified by King Rehoboam (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.10","r":"2Chr.11.10","rawR":"2Chr.11.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.10","value":"2Chr.11.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:10"},"). It was one of 65 cities claimed to have been conquered by the Egyptian pharaoh Shishak, who invaded Palestine around 924 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.2-12","r":"2Chr.12.2-12","rawR":"2Chr.12.2-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.12.2-12","value":"2Chr.12.2-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 12:2-12"},"). Much later, Aijalon was lost to the Philistines during the reign of Ahaz (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.28.18","r":"2Chr.28.18","rawR":"2Chr.28.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.28.18","value":"2Chr.28.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 28:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["The valley of Aijalon was part of the geographical setting of Joshua’s battle to control Gibeon (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.12","r":"Josh.10.12","rawR":"Josh.10.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.12","value":"Josh.10.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:12"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). To make the Israelite victory complete, God answered Joshua’s prayer to “let the sun stand still over Gibeon, and the moon over the valley of Aijalon” (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.12","r":"Josh.10.12","rawR":"Josh.10.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.12","value":"Josh.10.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of Refuge"},"; ",{"href":"?item=LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levitical Cities"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["2. City in the territory of Zebulun, burial place of the judge Elon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.12","r":"Judg.12.12","rawR":"Judg.12.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.12","value":"Judg.12.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 12:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Aijalon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.42","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.42","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.42"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.24","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.24","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:69","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.69","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.69","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.69"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:34-36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.34-36","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.34-36","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.34-36"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 14:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.31","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.31","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.13"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.10","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.10","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.10"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 12:2-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.12.2-12","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.12.2-12","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.12.2-12"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 28:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.28.18","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.28.18","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.28.18"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.12","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.12","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.12"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.12","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.12","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.12"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 12:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.12.12","rawQueryValue":"Judg.12.12","sourceRefExact":"Judg.12.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0102da954cc7993a2dfd724905954d2637eb4a6789700155d9264d9fff433ba8","sourceItemName":"Aijalon","sourceItemOrder":217,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Aijalon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Aijalon","title":"Aijalon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}